<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arima Yoriyuki</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1714">1714</a>–<a href="/years/1783">1783</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arima Yoriyuki was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurume">Kurume</a> Domain in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> and a noted mathematician of the Japanese wasan tradition. He published works on mathematics, including the Shuki Sanpo of 1769. His rule also saw a large peasant uprising against heavy taxes in 1754.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arima-yoriyuki.jpg" alt="Arima Yoriyuki" width="320" height="579" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arima_Yoriyuki.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
